.TH "XmeResolvePartOffsets" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmeResolvePartOffsets\fP \(em A widget writer function that computes the part offsets of a widget class
.iX "XmeResolvePartOffsets"
.iX "Xme functions" "XmeResolvePartOffsets"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/XmP\&.h>
\fBvoid \fBXmeResolvePartOffsets\fP\fR(
\fBWidgetClass \fBw_class\fR\fR,
\fBXmOffsetPtr *\fBoffset\fR\fR,
\fBXmOffsetPtr *\fBconstraint_offset\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%XmeResolvePartOffsets\fP lets a widget class be compiled without
the
sizes of its superclass parts, so that it keeps working when those
parts grow\&.  The class declares its resources with
\fB\%XmPartOffset\fP
(and its constraint resources with \fB\%XmConstraintPartOffset\fP)
instead
of \fB\%XtOffset\fP, and calls \fB\%XmeResolvePartOffsets\fP from its
class_initialize or class_part_initialize method\&.
.PP
It adds the sizes of the superclasses to the widget and constraint
sizes of \fIw_class\fP, aligned for any type; allocates and fills the
offset tables, which give for each class in the chain the offset of
its part in the instance and constraint records; and rewrites the
offsets of the resources and synthetic resources of the class\&.  The
widget then reaches its fields through the tables, with \fB\%XmField\fP
and \fB\%XmConstraintField\fP\&.
.IP "\fIw_class\fP" 10
Specifies the widget class\&.
.IP "\fIoffset\fP" 10
Returns the offset table of the instance record\&.
.IP "\fIconstraint_offset\fP" 10
Returns the offset table of the constraint record, or NULL if
\fIw_class\fP is not a Constraint subclass\&.  Pass NULL if the class
has no
constraint resources of its own\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmResolveAllPartOffsets\fP(3) and
\fB\%XmResolvePartOffsets\fP(3)\&.
